# freetype -- rasterises every glyph on the screen.
#
# --with-harfbuzz=no is a deliberate simplification. freetype and harfbuzz
# depend on each other: harfbuzz needs freetype to load a face, and freetype
# uses harfbuzz to improve auto-hinting of OpenType fonts. BLFS resolves this by
# building freetype twice, with harfbuzz in between.
#
# Duct builds it once, without. What is lost is auto-hinter quality on fonts
# that have no hinting instructions of their own -- a rendering nicety, not a
# capability. What is gained is that the build order stays a graph rather than a
# graph plus an exception. If the difference is ever judged to matter, the fix
# is a second pass, not a different library.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://downloads.sourceforge.net/freetype/freetype-2.13.3.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=0550350666d427c74daeb85d5ac7bb353acba5f76956395995311a9c6f063289
SRC_DIR=freetype-2.13.3

CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --with-harfbuzz=no --with-brotli=yes --enable-freetype-config"
